          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.97,
          "end": 5.73,
          "en": "-: So one solution is virtualization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.73,
          "end": 7.2,
          "en": "for our previous problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.2,
          "end": 9.87,
          "en": "So the problem is, when you build a software",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.87,
          "end": 12.6,
          "en": "or the application which works on your machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.6,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "it may not work on someone else machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.22,
          "en": "is because even if they do the configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.22,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "which consumes a lot of time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 20.964,
          "en": "in terms of installation configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.964,
          "end": 24.51,
          "en": "even if you do that, it might not work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 24.51,
          "end": 26.13,
          "en": "And to solve that problem, we are saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.13,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "okay, we can use something called virtualization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 30.84,
          "en": "Now, before we understand how we can solve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 30.84,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "the problem with virtualization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 35.55,
          "en": "let's understand, what is virtualization?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "So what happens is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "when you talk about your system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "so let's say any system in which you work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 41.82,
          "en": "even your mobile phone, or your desktop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 41.82,
          "end": 44.67,
          "en": "laptop, servers, they all do the same thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 44.67,
          "end": 47.64,
          "en": "What you have is you have a basic hardware, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 47.64,
          "end": 49.26,
          "en": "So you have a hardware layer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 49.26,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "Now this is your actual hardware, your CPU,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "RAM, motherboard, all the stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 58.11,
          "en": "Now, on top of this hardware, to make it work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 58.11,
          "end": 59.07,
          "en": "of course, as a user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 59.07,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "we will not be interacting with the hardware directly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 63.48,
          "en": "What you need in between is OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 63.48,
          "end": 65.07,
          "en": "Now, this is your operating system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 65.07,
          "end": 67.219,
          "en": "which can be Windows, Linux, Mac, doesn't matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 67.219,
          "end": 69.81,
          "en": "There are multiple OS options available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 71.88,
          "en": "So if you want to use your hardware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 71.88,
          "end": 73.47,
          "en": "the only way you can do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 73.47,
          "end": 75.66,
          "en": "is with the help of operating systems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 75.66,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "And that's why when you buy a laptop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "you get two things, not one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 79.669,
          "en": "You're not just buying a laptop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 79.669,
          "end": 81.377,
          "en": "you're buying Windows with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 81.377,
          "end": 83.43,
          "en": "Yeah, they say they give it for free,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 83.43,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "but you do pay for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 85.68,
          "en": "Okay, keeping that aside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 85.68,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "you got a hardware and you got an OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 88.17,
          "end": 91.92,
          "en": "Now, in real world, we directly don't use OS, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 92.97,
          "en": "We use software, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 92.97,
          "end": 94.8,
          "en": "if you want to add two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 94.8,
          "end": 97.32,
          "en": "you can't simply ask your OS to add two numbers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 98.75999999999999,
          "en": "you need a calculator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 98.75999999999999,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "Now you might be saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 101.94,
          "en": "hey, you know calculator you'll find in every device?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 101.94,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "Not exactly if, I don't know if you have used iPad,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 105.57,
          "en": "we don't have calculator there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 105.57,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "Anyway, but you can install it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 109.77000000000001,
          "en": "The point is, if you want to perform any operation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 109.77000000000001,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "you'll need a application or a software.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "And as a user, you use software,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 117.50999999999999,
          "en": "software talks to OS, OS talks to hardware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 117.50999999999999,
          "end": 118.59,
          "en": "That's how the flow is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 118.59,
          "end": 119.78999999999999,
          "en": "Now, let's say as a developer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 119.78999999999999,
          "end": 121.35,
          "en": "how will you use virtualization?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 121.35,
          "end": 123.69,
          "en": "So what you do is, if you want to use virtualization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 123.69,
          "end": 126.99,
          "en": "you will be installing another OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 126.99,
          "end": 128.34,
          "en": "Okay, now that's tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 128.34,
          "end": 130.86,
          "en": "How will you install two OS on the same machine?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 130.86,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "I mean, of course we can do dual boot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 134.43,
          "en": "where you have two OS in the same system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 134.43,
          "end": 137.82,
          "en": "but at one time you can use only one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 137.82,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "Something like if you have a laptop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 141.51,
          "en": "you can install Windows, or you can use Ubuntu,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 141.51,
          "end": 145.14600000000002,
          "en": "you can install both as a dual setup, or dual OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 145.14600000000002,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "but then you can use only one at a time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "In virtualization, you use two OS at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 152.223,
          "en": "What we do is, we have a hardware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 152.223,
          "end": 154.53,
          "en": "and then we install our OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 154.53,
          "end": 157.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now this is your host OS, the main OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 157.17000000000002,
          "end": 160.44,
          "en": "Now on top of it, you can install one more OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 160.44,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "But then how exactly it will work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 163.333,
          "en": "Because if you want to install,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 163.333,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "let's say you have a hardware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 165.935,
          "en": "you have a Windows on top of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 165.935,
          "end": 168.51,
          "en": "and now you want to use Ubuntu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 168.51,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "Now, when you try to install Ubuntu onto Windows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 172.77,
          "en": "Windows will say what are you doing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 172.77,
          "end": 174.32999999999998,
          "en": "You can't install OS and on our OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 174.32999999999998,
          "end": 178.41,
          "en": "So Ubuntu says, even if you install me, you need a hardware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 178.41,
          "end": 180,
          "en": "So what you do is you fake it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 180,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "You say, okay, what if you can fool Ubuntu by saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 186.15,
          "en": "you know, let me give you something in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 186.15,
          "end": 189.93,
          "en": "which is not a hardware, but it will behave like a hardware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 189.93,
          "end": 193.05,
          "en": "Now, that is your virtual hardware,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 193.05,
          "end": 195.33,
          "en": "or we can say virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 195.33,
          "end": 198.96,
          "en": "So you have a hardware, on top of that, you got a OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 198.96,
          "end": 201.9,
          "en": "on top of that, you got a machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 201.9,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "which is not a physical machine, but a virtual machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 205.35,
          "en": "which is actually a software",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 205.35,
          "end": 206.936,
          "en": "which fakes like it's a hardware.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 206.936,
          "end": 209.52,
          "en": "And then on top of that you can install Ubuntu.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 209.52,
          "end": 212.61,
          "en": "Now this is called virtualization,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 212.61,
          "end": 214.35,
          "en": "where you are installing an OS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 214.35,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "on a virtual hardware or a virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 217.54500000000002,
          "en": "And this concept is very famous, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 217.54500000000002,
          "end": 218.378,
          "en": "So if you talk about virtual machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 218.378,
          "end": 220.32,
          "en": "it's very famous, but the question is why.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 220.32,
          "end": 221.19,
          "en": "Now think about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 221.19,
          "end": 222.96,
          "en": "If you go back to our previous example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 222.96,
          "end": 224.7,
          "en": "of a previous problem of docker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 224.7,
          "end": 226.031,
          "en": "or not docker, but application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 226.031,
          "end": 228.909,
          "en": "When you build application on your machine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 228.909,
          "end": 231.54,
          "en": "which is there in your C: drive let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 234.69,
          "en": "or maybe on your OS, it's working on your machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 234.69,
          "end": 237.03,
          "en": "is because you have the required software,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 239.4,
          "en": "like a web server, database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 239.4,
          "end": 241.47,
          "en": "configuration, network components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 241.47,
          "end": 242.91,
          "en": "everything they're configured,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 242.91,
          "end": 244.8,
          "en": "and then you have application as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 244.8,
          "end": 246.6,
          "en": "Now when you want to give this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 246.6,
          "end": 248.34,
          "en": "to your colleague, or to your testing team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 248.34,
          "end": 249.9,
          "en": "or to your ops team,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 249.9,
          "end": 253.59,
          "en": "you can only give the software, not the entire OS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 253.59,
          "end": 255.51,
          "en": "But what if you can do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 255.51,
          "end": 257.19,
          "en": "Virtualization says you can do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 257.19,
          "end": 258.023,
          "en": "You know how?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 258.023,
          "end": 259.86,
          "en": "We have hardware, we got host OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 259.86,
          "end": 262.53,
          "en": "on top of that we have virtual machine OS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 262.53,
          "end": 263.49,
          "en": "or virtual machine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 263.49,
          "end": 265.02,
          "en": "So normally we can implement virtual machine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 265.02,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "with help of hypervisor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 269.91,
          "en": "And then on top of it, we can install Ubuntu, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 269.91,
          "end": 272.64,
          "en": "And on Ubuntu, you can build your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 272.64,
          "end": 273.69,
          "en": "It's OS right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 273.69,
          "end": 276.48,
          "en": "So, open Ubuntu, do all the things which you're doing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 276.48,
          "end": 279.36,
          "en": "you know, install your web server, install database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 279.36,
          "end": 282.307,
          "en": "do all the configuration, you have your running app there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 282.307,
          "end": 286.65,
          "en": "Now, you don't have to give just the software.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 286.65,
